	(text "State table (5-bit): 0 RESET, 1 WAIT_READY, 2 IDLE, 3 C1_START, 4 C1_WAIT, 5 P1_START, 6 P1_WAIT, 7 C2_START, 8 C2_WAIT, 9 P2_START, 10 P2_WAIT, 11 FC1_START, 12 FC1_WAIT, 13 FC2_START, 14 FC2_WAIT, 15 ARGMAX_START, 16 ARGMAX_WAIT, 17 FINISH, 18 WAIT_START_LOW, 19 ERROR."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 540 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5902f381-48e8-44ce-8af9-7049da877f77")
	)

	(text "Microcode address: A[4:0]=state, A5=START_S, A6=IMAGE_READY_S, A7=MODEL_READY_S, A8..A14=C1/P1/C2/P2/FC1/FC2/ARGMAX done, A15=TIMEOUT.\nMicrocode data: [4:0]=next state, 5=BUSY, 6=DONE, 7=RESULT_VALID_SET, 8=ERROR, [11:9]=STAGE_CODE, 12=TIMEOUT_CLR, 13=POOL_SEL, 14=FC_SEL, 15=spare.\nPOOL_SEL is high in P2 (states 9/10); FC_SEL is high in FC2 (states 13/14); both are held through the matching WAIT state so S05/S09 keep the phase.\nTIMEOUT_CLR is active-high in microcode; U16D inverts it for the 74HC161 ~PE input.\nThe 74HC688 outputs are active-low: U16E/U16F convert TIMEOUT_N and IDLE_N to active-high TIMEOUT_I/IDLE_MATCH."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 550 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "95e83a8b-5092-4ca1-b932-758d8168315c")
	)

	(text "Timeout: 24-bit counter (U18..U23) counts while BUSY; compares to 0xFFFFFF with U24..U26.  At 8 MHz the limit is ~2.1 s for the whole inference; a per-stage limit can be obtained by splitting TIMEOUT_CLR per stage."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 565 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6a2c1e24-57de-45ad-851e-3d05c1397d70")
	)

